  "surprise": "Systems mechanism confirmed, score not. Setup fell from 14-16 s to 3 s on every seed ('records on cuda after 3s'; first curve point at step 192/184/167 vs 153's step 1) and pretraining ran 4875/4907/4829 steps (mean 4870 vs 153-claude's 4503, +8.2%; registered 4,750-5,100, central 4,880), 4.31 epochs. Metric 650/674/652 (mean 659.33) vs 153-claude's 676/700/685 (687.00): -27.7, paired -26/-26/-33, inside the registered -35..+45 but far below the +8 central. Discard. The model and math are 153's (tokenized tensors torch.equal to 153's to_gpu on all 154,990 records; optimizer code is 160-claude's), so this is a +8% pretraining-steps ablation of the incumbent that scored lower on all three seeds. With 160-claude (+3% steps, 673) it gives no evidence that steps beyond ~4 epochs buy score: the fewer-steps losses of 146-claude/147-claude do not extend upward here. Seed 0 handed off a weak sampler: held-out greedy 0.931 (s1/s2 0.976/0.972; 153 0.9675) and round-1 solved 259/1500 at acc 0.072 (153 s0: 766 at 0.271), recovering to 1111 by round 4; round-4 solved 1111/1164/1145 (mean 1140 vs 153 s0 1157). Val loss 0.0848/0.0820/0.0826 (153: 0.0883). Untested reading: at LR floor 0.3 the handoff iterate depends on the last few length-homogeneous token-budget batches (153's val loss swings 0.069-0.095 between curve points), so a different step count lands elsewhere on that oscillation; the difference of two 3-seed means has sd ~36, so -28 is also within noise. The 3 s setup is a free, identical-data speedup that a future keep could carry.",
